  "worked_solution": "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(W)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W))$, we reduce $W$ to row echelon form, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 18 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and  $1$\n non-pivot column (the $2$nd). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(W)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W))=1.\n$$",
